{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfPz4b9kNBy4Tc6NH5v1J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LcDmQbRtv8hUaR9r4msUvv","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement BE-005 changes","subagent_type":"implementer","prompt":"Three changes to `sample-service`, shipped together on one branch. They touch the order,\nshipment and customer features and the shared `api` package.\n\n## 1. Partial fulfilment\n\nAn order is for a quantity of goods, and that quantity is shipped in parts. Today an order\nhas no quantity, a shipment carries no quantity, and nothing records how much of an order\nits shipments account for.\n\n- An order gains a `quantity`: a positive integer, `1` when the request does not give one.\n  A quantity below `1` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the field. `GET /orders/{orderId}`\n  reports it.\n- A shipment gains a `quantity` with the same rule and the same default.\n- An order's shipments **allocate** its quantity. `POST /shipments` is rejected with HTTP 409,\n  and nothing changes, when the shipment would push the order's allocated quantity above the\n  order's quantity. The allocated quantity is the sum over the order's shipments that are not\n  `CANCELLED`. Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current\n  behaviour.\n- Shipments gain transitions: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` moves `CREATED` to\n  `CONFIRMED`; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver` moves `CONFIRMED` to `DELIVERED`, a new\n  status; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel` moves `CREATED` to `CANCELLED`. Each returns\n  the shipment. Any other transition is rejected with HTTP 409 and changes nothing; an\n  unknown shipment is rejected with HTTP 404.\n- An order gains a fulfilment status, reported by `GET /orders/{orderId}` and by the list as\n  `fulfilment: { allocated, delivered, status }`. A newly created order is `UNALLOCATED`.\n  `delivered` is the sum over the order's `DELIVERED` shipments. The status is `DELIVERED`\n  when `delivered` reaches the order's quantity, `FULLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` reaches\n  it, `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` is above zero and below it, and `UNALLOCATED`\n  otherwise.\n- `GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS` lists only the orders in that status. Without the parameter\n  the list is unchanged. A value that is not a fulfilment status is rejected with HTTP 400\n  naming the parameter.\n- **Cancelling a shipment releases its quantity.** After the cancel, the order's fulfilment no\n  longer counts that shipment, its status moves back accordingly, and a new shipment for the\n  released quantity is accepted.\n- **An order's quantity can be amended after shipments exist.** `PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity`\n  with `{ \"quantity\": n }` sets it, under the same positive-integer rule (HTTP 400 naming the\n  field); an unknown order is HTTP 404. The amendment is rejected with HTTP 409, and nothing\n  changes, when the new quantity is below the order's allocated quantity. After an amendment the\n  order's fulfilment reflects the new quantity: an order that was `FULLY_ALLOCATED` at 4 is\n  `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` at 6, and its shipments then allocate against 6.\n\n## 2. An order needs its customer\n\nToday `POST /orders` accepts any `customerId`. From now on an order for a customer that does\nnot exist is rejected with HTTP 422 through the error envelope. `GET /customers/{customerId}`\nfor an unknown customer reports HTTP 404 **through the error envelope**, like orders and\nshipments already do.\n\nThe existing `OrderControllerTest` creates orders for a customer that was never created.\nUpdate it so that the suite reflects the new rule.\n\n## 3. Paged lists\n\n`GET /customers`, `GET /orders` and `GET /shipments` accept `limit` (1 to 100, default 100)\nand `offset` (0 or more, default 0), and slice the list in id order. The response body stays\nthe array it is today, so callers that do not page keep working, and every list response\ncarries the total number of items before slicing in an `X-Total-Count` header. A `limit`\noutside its range or a negative `offset` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the parameter. On\n`GET /orders` the total is the total after the `fulfilment` filter.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture must be preserved.\n- Do not add new dependencies.\n- Do not modify files outside the order, shipment and customer features and the shared `api`\n  package, except tests.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Existing build passes.\n2. Existing tests pass, other than `OrderControllerTest`, which this ticket changes.\n3. Quantities, allocation, the three transitions, the fulfilment read model and the filter\n   behave as specified, including the release of a cancelled shipment's quantity and the\n   amendment of an order's quantity.\n4. Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API.\n5. An order for an unknown customer is refused; every list pages as specified and unpaged\n   calls are unchanged.\n6. No new Maven dependency appears.\n7. No unrelated production file changes.\n\n---\n\n## Planner's handoff\n\nBased on my analysis of the repository structure and the ticket requirements, here is the mapping of all read paths with their values, storage, and computation locations:\n\n## Read Paths\n\n| Path | Value | Stored or Computed | Where Computed |\n|------|-------|-------------------|-----------------|\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | orderId | stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | customerId | stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | amount | stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | currency | stored | Order entity |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | quantity | stored | Order entity (new field, default 1) |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | fulfilment.allocated | computed | OrderController/OrderService - sums non-CANCELLED shipment quantities for that order |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | fulfilment.delivered | computed | OrderController/OrderService - sums DELIVERED shipment quantities for that order |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | fulfilment.status | computed | OrderController/OrderService - compares allocated and delivered against order quantity |\n| GET /orders?[limit=X]&amp;[offset=Y]&amp;[fulfilment=STATUS] | order array (per above) | stored/computed (mixed) | per above |\n| GET /orders?[limit=X]&amp;[offset=Y]&amp;[fulfilment=STATUS] | X-Total-Count header | computed | OrderRepository.findAll() or new paginated method - counts total after fulfilment filter before slicing |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | shipmentId | stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | orderId | stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | carrier | stored | Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | status | stored | Shipment entity (extended to include DELIVERED) |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | quantity | stored | Shipment entity (new field, default 1) |\n| GET /shipments?[limit=X]&amp;[offset=Y] | shipment array (per above) | stored (mixed) | per above |\n| GET /shipments?[limit=X]&amp;[offset=Y] | X-Total-Count header | computed | ShipmentRepository.findAll() or new paginated method - counts total before slicing |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | customerId | stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | name | stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | email | stored | Customer entity |\n| GET /customers?[limit=X]&amp;[offset=Y] | customer array (per above) | stored | per above |\n| GET /customers?[limit=X]&amp;[offset=Y] | X-Total-Count header | computed | CustomerRepository.findAll() or new paginated method - counts total before slicing |\n\n## Shape\n\nEach list endpoint (GET /orders, GET /shipments, GET /customers) returns the array of entity objects as the response body with optional query parameters `limit` (1-100, default 100) and `offset` (0+, default 0), while an X-Total-Count response header carries the total count before pagination. Order fulfilment status is filtered via optional `fulfilment` query parameter on GET /orders, filtering the result set and affecting the X-Total-Count accordingly. Atomic entity fields (orderId, customerId, carrier, etc.) are stored in their respective entity tables; aggregate values like fulfilment status and allocated/delivered sums are computed on read by joining or querying related shipment records.\n\n## Unresolved\n\nNo paths remain unresolved. All read paths map to values that are either explicitly stored in the entity classes (Order, Shipment, Customer—with new fields quantity added per the ticket) or computed by aggregating or deriving from stored data (fulfilment status from shipment summation, X-Total-Count from repository counting before slice, status transitions for shipments from explicit state changes).\n\n**Relevant file paths:**\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderRepository.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/Customer.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerController.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerRepository.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2440,"cache_read_input_tokens":9551,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2440},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1bd79e49-f141-44f7-9deb-c27270448e07","uuid":"60e405df-a788-427f-b21b-089000c5ebc1","timestamp":"2026-09-25T10:17:23.332Z","request_id":"req_011CfPz4aMdBr8i58GZBsZ8R","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LcDmQbRtv8hUaR9r4msUvv":{"description":"Implement BE-005 changes","subagent_type":"implementer","prompt":"Three changes to `sample-service`, shipped together on one branch. They touch the order,\nshipment and customer features and the shared `api` package.\n\n## 1. Partial fulfilment\n\nAn order is for a quantity of go