{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a267bb68e29d63594","tool_use_id":"toolu_012t9mojqG6KNaKQw3Fo778i","description":"Verify BE-005 implementation","subagent_type":"verifier","is_backgrounded":true,"spawn_depth":1,"task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Three changes to `sample-service`, shipped together on one branch. They touch the order,\nshipment and customer features and the shared `api` package.\n\n## 1. Partial fulfilment\n\nAn order is for a quantity of goods, and that quantity is shipped in parts. Today an order\nhas no quantity, a shipment carries no quantity, and nothing records how much of an order\nits shipments account for.\n\n- An order gains a `quantity`: a positive integer, `1` when the request does not give one.\n  A quantity below `1` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the field. `GET /orders/{orderId}`\n  reports it.\n- A shipment gains a `quantity` with the same rule and the same default.\n- An order's shipments **allocate** its quantity. `POST /shipments` is rejected with HTTP 409,\n  and nothing changes, when the shipment would push the order's allocated quantity above the\n  order's quantity. The allocated quantity is the sum over the order's shipments that are not\n  `CANCELLED`. Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current\n  behaviour.\n- Shipments gain transitions: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` moves `CREATED` to\n  `CONFIRMED`; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver` moves `CONFIRMED` to `DELIVERED`, a new\n  status; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel` moves `CREATED` to `CANCELLED`. Each returns\n  the shipment. Any other transition is rejected with HTTP 409 and changes nothing; an\n  unknown shipment is rejected with HTTP 404.\n- An order gains a fulfilment status, reported by `GET /orders/{orderId}` and by the list as\n  `fulfilment: { allocated, delivered, status }`. A newly created order is `UNALLOCATED`.\n  `delivered` is the sum over the order's `DELIVERED` shipments. The status is `DELIVERED`\n  when `delivered` reaches the order's quantity, `FULLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` reaches\n  it, `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` is above zero and below it, and `UNALLOCATED`\n  otherwise.\n- `GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS` lists only the orders in that status. Without the parameter\n  the list is unchanged. A value that is not a fulfilment status is rejected with HTTP 400\n  naming the parameter.\n- **Cancelling a shipment releases its quantity.** After the cancel, the order's fulfilment no\n  longer counts that shipment, its status moves back accordingly, and a new shipment for the\n  released quantity is accepted.\n- **An order's quantity can be amended after shipments exist.** `PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity`\n  with `{ \"quantity\": n }` sets it, under the same positive-integer rule (HTTP 400 naming the\n  field); an unknown order is HTTP 404. The amendment is rejected with HTTP 409, and nothing\n  changes, when the new quantity is below the order's allocated quantity. After an amendment the\n  order's fulfilment reflects the new quantity: an order that was `FULLY_ALLOCATED` at 4 is\n  `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` at 6, and its shipments then allocate against 6.\n\n## 2. An order needs its customer\n\nToday `POST /orders` accepts any `customerId`. From now on an order for a customer that does\nnot exist is rejected with HTTP 422 through the error envelope. `GET /customers/{customerId}`\nfor an unknown customer reports HTTP 404 **through the error envelope**, like orders and\nshipments already do.\n\nThe existing `OrderControllerTest` creates orders for a customer that was never created.\nUpdate it so that the suite reflects the new rule.\n\n## 3. Paged lists\n\n`GET /customers`, `GET /orders` and `GET /shipments` accept `limit` (1 to 100, default 100)\nand `offset` (0 or more, default 0), and slice the list in id order. The response body stays\nthe array it is today, so callers that do not page keep working, and every list response\ncarries the total number of items before slicing in an `X-Total-Count` header. A `limit`\noutside its range or a negative `offset` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the parameter. On\n`GET /orders` the total is the total after the `fulfilment` filter.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture must be preserved.\n- Do not add new dependencies.\n- Do not modify files outside the order, shipment and customer features and the shared `api`\n  package, except tests.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Existing build passes.\n2. Existing tests pass, other than `OrderControllerTest`, which this ticket changes.\n3. Quantities, allocation, the three transitions, the fulfilment read model and the filter\n   behave as specified, including the release of a cancelled shipment's quantity and the\n   amendment of an order's quantity.\n4. Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API.\n5. An order for an unknown customer is refused; every list pages as specified and unpaged\n   calls are unchanged.\n6. No new Maven dependency appears.\n7. No unrelated production file changes.\n\n---\n\n## Implementer's handoff\n\nExcellent! All tests pass. Let me provide the final handoff summary.\n\n## Handoff\n\n### Changed\n\n**API Exceptions** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt`)\n- Added `UnprocessableEntityException` class for HTTP 422 errors (semantic validation, not addressing)\n\n**API Error Codes** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt`)\n- Added `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` error code for 422 errors when orders reference non-existent customers\n\n**Order Entity** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt`)\n- Added `quantity` field (default 1) to Order data class\n- Added `OrderFulfilment` data class with allocated, delivered, and status fields\n- Added `FulfilmentStatus` enum (UNALLOCATED, PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED, FULLY_ALLOCATED, DELIVERED)\n- Added `UpdateQuantityRequest` for PUT endpoint\n\n**Shipment Entity** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt`)\n- Added `quantity` field (default 1) to Shipment data class\n- Added `DELIVERED` status to `ShipmentStatus` enum\n\n**OrderController** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt`)\n- Validates customer exists (throws 422 if not) when creating orders\n- Validates order quantity (default 1, rejects if < 1)\n- Added `PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity` endpoint for quantity amendment with allocation validation\n- Injects shipment repository for fulfillment computation\n- Modified `GET /orders` to support `limit`, `offset`, and `fulfilment` query parameters with validation\n- Computes fulfillment status (allocated, delivered, status) for each order on read\n- Enriches all order responses with computed fulfillment data\n\n**ShipmentController** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt`)\n- Validates shipment quantity (default 1, rejects if < 1)\n- Validates allocation constraint when creating shipments (409 if would exceed order quantity)\n- Added `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` transition (CREATED → CONFIRMED)\n- Added `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver` transition (CONFIRMED → DELIVERED)\n- Added `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel` transition (CREATED → CANCELLED)\n- Modified `GET /shipments` to support `limit` and `offset` pagination with validation\n- Returns X-Total-Count header with total count before pagination\n\n**CustomerController** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerController.kt`)\n- Changed `GET /{customerId}` to throw `ResourceNotFoundException` through error envelope instead of `ResponseEntity.notFound()`\n- Modified `GET /customers` to support `limit` and `offset` pagination with validation\n- Returns X-Total-Count header with total count before pagination\n\n**ShipmentRepository** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt`)\n- Added `findByOrderId()` method to retrieve shipments for an order (used for fulfillment computation)\n\n**OrderControllerTest** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderControllerTest.kt`)\n- Now creates test customer before each test (ensures customer exists)\n- Added 14 new tests covering: quantity validation, customer validation (422), fulfillment status computation, quantity amendment, pagination, and fulfillment filtering\n\n**ShipmentControllerTest** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt`)\n- Now creates test order with quantity=10 before each test\n- Added 13 new tests covering: quantity validation, allocation validation, transitions (confirm/deliver/cancel), invalid state transitions, and pagination\n\n**CustomerControllerTest** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerControllerTest.kt`)\n- Updated existing test to verify error envelope on 404 for unknown customer\n- Added 4 new tests covering: pagination, X-Total-Count header, and invalid pagination parameters\n\n### Against Planner's Read-Path Table\n\n| Path | Value | Implementation Status |\n|------|-------|----------------------|\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | orderId, customerId, amount, currency, quantity | Stored in Order entity, returned in response |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | fulfilment.allocated, delivered, status | Computed by OrderController, aggregating shipments |\n| GET /orders?[limit]&[offset]&[fulfilment] | order array | Implemented with pagination and filtering |\n| GET /orders?[limit]&[offset]&[fulfilment] | X-Total-Count header | Computed before pagination slice |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | shipmentId, orderId, carrier, status, quantity | Stored in Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments?[limit]&[offset] | shipment array | Implemented with pagination |\n| GET /shipments?[limit]&[offset] | X-Total-Count header | Computed before pagination slice |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | customerId, name, email | Stored in Customer entity |\n| GET /customers?[limit]&[offset] | customer array | Implemented with pagination |\n| GET /customers?[limit]&[offset] | X-Total-Count header | Computed before pagination slice |\n\n### Disagreed\n\nNone. Code implementation matches planner's table exactly.\n\n### Tests\n\n**OrderControllerTest** (18 tests total):\n- Baseline tests (existing functionality preserved): create order, read order, 404 error envelope, duplicate order error\n- New quantity tests: default quantity of 1, explicit quantity, invalid quantity rejection\n- New customer validation test: 422 error for non-existent customer\n- New fulfillment tests: initial UNALLOCATED status\n- New quantity amendment tests: successful amendment, invalid quantity rejection, rejection below allocated\n- New pagination tests: limit/offset slicing, X-Total-Count header, invalid limit/offset\n- New filtering tests: fulfillment status filter, invalid status rejection\n\n**ShipmentControllerTest** (18 tests total):\n- Baseline tests (existing functionality preserved): create shipment, duplicate rejection, read shipment, 404 error, list in order\n- New quantity tests: default quantity of 1, explicit quantity, invalid quantity rejection\n- New allocation validation test: rejects shipment that would exceed order quantity\n- New state transition tests: confirm (CREATED→CONFIRMED), deliver (CONFIRMED→DELIVERED), cancel (CREATED→CANCELLED)\n- New invalid transition tests: cannot confirm non-CREATED, cannot deliver non-CONFIRMED, cannot cancel non-CREATED\n- New pagination tests: limit/offset slicing, X-Total-Count header, invalid limit rejection\n\n**CustomerControllerTest** (7 tests total):\n- Baseline tests (existing functionality preserved): create customer, read customer, 404 error envelope\n- New pagination tests: limit/offset slicing, X-Total-Count header, invalid limit/offset rejection\n\n### Verification\n\n```\nTests run: 44, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\n\nAll 44 tests pass, covering:\n1. Quantity fields and validation for orders and shipments (default 1, reject if < 1)\n2. Customer validation (422 error when order references non-existent customer)\n3. Allocation constraint enforcement (409 when shipment would exceed order quantity)\n4. Shipment state transitions (confirm, deliver, cancel with 409 for invalid transitions)\n5. Fulfillment status computation (UNALLOCATED → PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED → FULLY_ALLOCATED → DELIVERED)\n6. Pagination with X-Total-Count header on all list endpoints\n7. Pagination parameter validation (limit 1-100, offset ≥ 0)\n8. Fulfillment status filtering on GET /orders\n9. Quantity amendment with allocation constraint validation\n10. Error envelope consistency through 404 for unknown customers\n\n### Not Done\n\nNone. All requirements from the ticket have been implemented and tested.","uuid":"f3c24849-d7e6-44a6-9642-a61d544ee838","session_id":"1bd79e49-f141-44f7-9deb-c27270448e07"}
