 and `offset` pagination with validation\n- Returns X-Total-Count header with total count before pagination\n\n**ShipmentRepository** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt`)\n- Added `findByOrderId()` method to retrieve shipments for an order (used for fulfillment computation)\n\n**OrderControllerTest** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderControllerTest.kt`)\n- Now creates test customer before each test (ensures customer exists)\n- Added 14 new tests covering: quantity validation, customer validation (422), fulfillment status computation, quantity amendment, pagination, and fulfillment filtering\n\n**ShipmentControllerTest** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt`)\n- Now creates test order with quantity=10 before each test\n- Added 13 new tests covering: quantity validation, allocation validation, transitions (confirm/deliver/cancel), invalid state transitions, and pagination\n\n**CustomerControllerTest** (`/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerControllerTest.kt`)\n- Updated existing test to verify error envelope on 404 for unknown customer\n- Added 4 new tests covering: pagination, X-Total-Count header, and invalid pagination parameters\n\n### Against Planner's Read-Path Table\n\n| Path | Value | Implementation Status |\n|------|-------|----------------------|\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | orderId, customerId, amount, currency, quantity | Stored in Order entity, returned in response |\n| GET /orders/{orderId} | fulfilment.allocated, delivered, status | Computed by OrderController, aggregating shipments |\n| GET /orders?[limit]&[offset]&[fulfilment] | order array | Implemented with pagination and filtering |\n| GET /orders?[limit]&[offset]&[fulfilment] | X-Total-Count header | Computed before pagination slice |\n| GET /shipments/{shipmentId} | shipmentId, orderId, carrier, status, quantity | Stored in Shipment entity |\n| GET /shipments?[limit]&[offset] | shipment array | Implemented with pagination |\n| GET /shipments?[limit]&[offset] | X-Total-Count header | Computed before pagination slice |\n| GET /customers/{customerId} | customerId, name, email | Stored in Customer entity |\n| GET /customers?[limit]&[offset] | customer array | Implemented with pagination |\n| GET /customers?[limit]&[offset] | X-Total-Count header | Computed before pagination slice |\n\n### Disagreed\n\nNone. Code implementation matches planner's table exactly.\n\n### Tests\n\n**OrderControllerTest** (18 tests total):\n- Baseline tests (existing functionality preserved): create order, read order, 404 error envelope, duplicate order error\n- New quantity tests: default quantity of 1, explicit quantity, invalid quantity rejection\n- New customer validation test: 422 error for non-existent customer\n- New fulfillment tests: initial UNALLOCATED status\n- New quantity amendment tests: successful amendment, invalid quantity rejection, rejection below allocated\n- New pagination tests: limit/offset slicing, X-Total-Count header, invalid limit/offset\n- New filtering tests: fulfillment status filter, invalid status rejection\n\n**ShipmentControllerTest** (18 tests total):\n- Baseline tests (existing functionality preserved): create shipment, duplicate rejection, read shipment, 404 error, list in order\n- New quantity tests: default quantity of 1, explicit quantity, invalid quantity rejection\n- New allocation validation test: rejects shipment that would exceed order quantity\n- New state transition tests: confirm (CREATED→CONFIRMED), deliver (CONFIRMED→DELIVERED), cancel (CREATED→CANCELLED)\n- New invalid transition tests: cannot confirm non-CREATED, cannot deliver non-CONFIRMED, cannot cancel non-CREATED\n- New pagination tests: limit/offset slicing, X-Total-Count header, invalid limit rejection\n\n**CustomerControllerTest** (7 tests total):\n- Baseline tests (existing functionality preserved): create customer, read customer, 404 error envelope\n- New pagination tests: limit/offset slicing, X-Total-Count header, invalid limit/offset rejection\n\n### Verification\n\n```\nTests run: 44, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\n\nAll 44 tests pass, covering:\n1. Quantity fields and validation for orders and shipments (default 1, reject if < 1)\n2. Customer validation (422 error when order references non-existent customer)\n3. Allocation constraint enforcement (409 when shipment would exceed order quantity)\n4. Shipment state transitions (confirm, deliver, cancel with 409 for invalid transitions)\n5. Fulfillment status computation (UNALLOCATED → PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED → FULLY_ALLOCATED → DELIVERED)\n6. Pagination with X-Total-Count header on all list endpoints\n7. Pagination parameter validation (limit 1-100, offset ≥ 0)\n8. Fulfillment status filtering on GET /orders\n9. Quantity amendment with allocation constraint validation\n10. Error envelope consistency through 404 for unknown customers\n\n### Not Done\n\nNone. All requirements from the ticket have been implemented and tested.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-private-var-folders-jr-lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn-T-observatory-run-da7c45c9-b121-4aed-8b9e-41df157ea4c1/1bd79e49-f141-44f7-9deb-c27270448e07/tasks/a267bb68e29d63594.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
